<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><generator uri="https://jekyllrb.com/" version="4.4.1">Jekyll</generator><link href="https://erikawa-e.github.io/lab-hp/feed.xml" rel="self" type="application/atom+xml"/><link href="https://erikawa-e.github.io/lab-hp/" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/><updated>2026-04-21T15:30:37+00:00</updated><id>https://erikawa-e.github.io/lab-hp/feed.xml</id><title type="html">FEBQI</title><entry><title type="html">Great news to share</title><link href="https://erikawa-e.github.io/lab-hp/blog/2026/hochan-award/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Great news to share"/><published>2026-03-25T15:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-03-25T15:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://erikawa-e.github.io/lab-hp/blog/2026/hochan-award</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://erikawa-e.github.io/lab-hp/blog/2026/hochan-award/"><![CDATA[<p>Hochan Chung (Research Trainee) has received the Best Bachelor’s Thesis Award. Congratulations, Hochan!</p> <p><img src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/a/AVvXsEh6uFVcUVnrVxX-29Ky0rdKEePieCmJMU_c5RJO5yXpRTWsEMJOUox1zs5SPDcPqP1HtRqRlSMedkAphWdosBjweYdRiP59J7-n9dsGGHIRggpzaZDvGB6DcLZoi9B0wxF_9Q_qzt-Ot5df9WVIIiagxsqPkwH5H6zBW-gn1zxpnpJkUxbd8GRhEIIbhNyM" alt="Hochan award"/></p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="news"/><category term="award"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Hochan Chung receives Best Bachelor's Thesis Award]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Birthdays</title><link href="https://erikawa-e.github.io/lab-hp/blog/2026/birthdays/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Birthdays"/><published>2026-03-10T15:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-03-10T15:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://erikawa-e.github.io/lab-hp/blog/2026/birthdays</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://erikawa-e.github.io/lab-hp/blog/2026/birthdays/"><![CDATA[<p>Oleksiy turned 80 (and Erika half that)! Happy birthday to both!</p> <p><img src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEj9OueJAp3siWIZLxym-Unn1V-djB60k74J2o40JhkW-aBDARdlaIZILHnG2U5E0vIUjOrWIiMFlJTpuVsfJ1lHkFPF6eeaA2k7k136aGLg1oehMtOQ33E5UcioAD_3Ac-wNPa5RuJbM42Bz9WYbY_z7tKJKVF09Ewluenc7BY5cGRdzfJXyWOlpcTLrZlL/s320/BD.png" alt="Birthday"/></p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="news"/><category term="lab-life"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Celebrating birthdays in the lab]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Our Review Article on Quantum Computing Published in a French Alumni Magazine</title><link href="https://erikawa-e.github.io/lab-hp/blog/2026/french-review-article/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Our Review Article on Quantum Computing Published in a French Alumni Magazine"/><published>2026-01-21T15:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-01-21T15:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://erikawa-e.github.io/lab-hp/blog/2026/french-review-article</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://erikawa-e.github.io/lab-hp/blog/2026/french-review-article/"><![CDATA[<p>A review article on quantum computing by Tetsuyoshi Yamada, Thomas Giovansili, and Erika Kawakami has been published in a French alumni magazine. Great outreach work!</p> <p><img src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/a/AVvXsEiuEfwxwy-viuGSJzS-RMvRhtKVNJyUHq3-MU5BGHXZ-82Oi8IinOAzcoafmJXfVdzh4jnpNSAK1LZSB9mJ3Pk4ta4Y_3vomPeRFMvzXveMZsso5HPl8PRooSg2nuUB9aqbQgsLikKP-FyQ-PineW5ydyfwqhvycOnCXBZp_r73qI3eRR7U67bw5DbE5Glp" alt="French article"/></p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="news"/><category term="publication"/><category term="outreach"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Review article by Yamada, Giovansili, and Kawakami published in French alumni magazine]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Great news to share</title><link href="https://erikawa-e.github.io/lab-hp/blog/2026/poster-award-prl-news/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Great news to share"/><published>2026-01-18T15:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-01-18T15:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://erikawa-e.github.io/lab-hp/blog/2026/poster-award-prl-news</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://erikawa-e.github.io/lab-hp/blog/2026/poster-award-prl-news/"><![CDATA[<p>Two pieces of great news: Hochan Chung received a poster award at the 2nd Quantum Technology Interdisciplinary Exchange Conference, and our PRL paper was featured in RIKEN Research News!</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="news"/><category term="award"/><category term="publication"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Poster award and PRL paper featured in RIKEN Research News]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">International collaborative project</title><link href="https://erikawa-e.github.io/lab-hp/blog/2025/jst-aspire/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="International collaborative project"/><published>2025-12-14T15:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2025-12-14T15:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://erikawa-e.github.io/lab-hp/blog/2025/jst-aspire</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://erikawa-e.github.io/lab-hp/blog/2025/jst-aspire/"><![CDATA[<p>Our project “Realization of Spin Qubits Using Floating Electrons on Solid Neon” has been selected for the JST ASPIRE program, launching an international collaboration with researchers in Germany and the USA!</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="news"/><category term="funding"/><category term="collaboration"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[JST ASPIRE project selected for international collaboration]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Tetsu’s farewell party</title><link href="https://erikawa-e.github.io/lab-hp/blog/2025/tetsu-farewell/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Tetsu’s farewell party"/><published>2025-09-15T15:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2025-09-15T15:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://erikawa-e.github.io/lab-hp/blog/2025/tetsu-farewell</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://erikawa-e.github.io/lab-hp/blog/2025/tetsu-farewell/"><![CDATA[<p>We held a farewell party for Tetsuyoshi Yamada. Thank you, Tetsu, for your contributions to the team!</p> <p><img src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/a/AVvXsEhHyhAJHoDQ_ekjfv7LYr9FcNL_eFExvNH5r73sSVgTlbh5s2m4T3NhMby5jGyhpLbiF9QVbk7FuHcnhvsQgZYc3wRcIgrBrMQo_GnTsC3FL6ryR45bgDz4HqkCbKnkg-5HNVgx6FxGdvm6QTTKQdOpsyVPHKl8yrLWwJnm5AtjxDrPLmT9jrYOnjKw9P2P" alt="Tetsu farewell"/></p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="news"/><category term="lab-life"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Farewell party for Tetsuyoshi Yamada]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Great News to Share</title><link href="https://erikawa-e.github.io/lab-hp/blog/2025/prl-editors-suggestion/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Great News to Share"/><published>2025-08-24T15:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2025-08-24T15:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://erikawa-e.github.io/lab-hp/blog/2025/prl-editors-suggestion</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://erikawa-e.github.io/lab-hp/blog/2025/prl-editors-suggestion/"><![CDATA[<p>Our Rydberg detection paper has been published in PRL and selected as an <strong>Editors’ Suggestion</strong> — only six papers were chosen! Additionally, Ash received a poster award at the LT30 conference. Congratulations to the team!</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="news"/><category term="publication"/><category term="award"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[PRL paper selected as Editors' Suggestion and poster award at LT30]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Sander’s Farewell party</title><link href="https://erikawa-e.github.io/lab-hp/blog/2024/sander-farewell/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Sander’s Farewell party"/><published>2024-08-01T15:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2024-08-01T15:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://erikawa-e.github.io/lab-hp/blog/2024/sander-farewell</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://erikawa-e.github.io/lab-hp/blog/2024/sander-farewell/"><![CDATA[<p>Thank you for your contribution to TDO, Sander! We wish you all the best!</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="news"/><category term="lab-life"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Farewell party for Sander van Haagen]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">FCP workshop at OIST</title><link href="https://erikawa-e.github.io/lab-hp/blog/2024/fcp-workshop-oist/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="FCP workshop at OIST"/><published>2024-06-06T15:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2024-06-06T15:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://erikawa-e.github.io/lab-hp/blog/2024/fcp-workshop-oist</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://erikawa-e.github.io/lab-hp/blog/2024/fcp-workshop-oist/"><![CDATA[<p>We all presented posters and gave talks at the FCP workshop on quantum technology at OIST. Thanks to the organizers for a great event!</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="news"/><category term="conference"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Team presents at quantum technology workshop at OIST]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Cherry blossoms burst into bloom at RIKEN</title><link href="https://erikawa-e.github.io/lab-hp/blog/2024/cherry-blossoms-2024/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Cherry blossoms burst into bloom at RIKEN"/><published>2024-04-02T15:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2024-04-02T15:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://erikawa-e.github.io/lab-hp/blog/2024/cherry-blossoms-2024</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://erikawa-e.github.io/lab-hp/blog/2024/cherry-blossoms-2024/"><![CDATA[<p>Spring has arrived at RIKEN! The cherry blossoms are in full bloom on the Wako campus.</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="news"/><category term="lab-life"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Spring cherry blossoms at RIKEN Wako campus]]></summary></entry></feed>